My first ascension was a Wizard, and this time I decided to try a
Tourist for a change. Artiwishless, colourless, polyless, polyselfless,
genoless, conflictless and AoLS-less are the default for me, so I kept
to them. This one was 68K turns, 2K turns faster than the Wiz.

+ Done the protection racket using credit cloning in minetown shops.

+ Soko had an amulet of reflection.

+ Blessed and rubbed a magic lamp. Wished for blessed +3 GDSM, got it.
A throne wish went for speed boots.

- Bags of holding and magic whistles seemed to be completely missing
from this game. Not being burdened meant making lots of stashes.

+ Ate tengu, got teleportitis (uncontrolled for 7K turns until another
tengu). Leashes get really useful.

+ Got permanent invisibility and see invisible by a !oI and
a stalker for a snack. Two intrinsics at the price of one.

+ After 40K turns, going without a magic whistle became too tedious.
Another blessed magic lamp wish went for it.

- Undeliberately ate a soldier instead of his ration and got aggravate
monster.

- The castle wand was 0:1. That sucked somewhat.

+ A pet purple worm (the most promising one, raised on VotD wraiths)
died unexpectedly. The castle wand wish went for a wand of undead
turning.
Status of Blurp II (neutral):  Level 42  HP 336(336)  AC 6, tame.

+ At 52K turns, not having a bag of holding started sucking really
hard. Wished for.

+ Sacrificing and praying gave me Vorpy. One less concern on Astral.

+ An arch-lich kindly donated an athame.

+ Mind flayers were somewhat scary as usual, especially if summoned
next to you. I was intending to max out Int on them, but it turned out
to be my purple worms' Int mostly:)

+ Made 110 blessed rustproof +5 darts:)

+ The last 2 wishes went for magic markers for enchant foo and (later)
gold detection.

- Undeliberately killed my purple worm by a death ray bounce on Earth.
Note to self to NEVER bring pets to the planes...

The Planes were somewhat nonstandard: I had forgotten to write ?oGD,
and the PYEC was ignoring me, so I had to wield the Amulet and zap
/oSDD. The portal to Air was somewhat unexpected, and I got there
without levitation. Air elementals were asking to be polymorphed as
usual. I recharged my last magic marker as soon as I could, and wrote
the two ?oGD so Fire and Water were easier.

On Astral I visited the central altar with Famine first (darts were
handy as there was plenty of them, and I didn't have to pick them all
up to reload), which turned out to be lawful. The next visit was to
Death on the left (he touched me a couple of times, but with 200+ HP,
nobody notices:) ). Kicked some Rogue ass, got a fake amulet for a
souvenir. There was an Archon (which wasn't too tough), and the altar
was neutral. The shameful thing was that I had intended to take
pictures of the Riders I met, but forgot to do that. I still have a
photo of a wood nymph, but she's wearing a mummy wrapping there:).

